W166 native observer compatibility change:
- Current Yandex builds may expose Media player properties but omit CDP kUrl.
- When kUrl is absent, use a passive, read-only fallback tied to the exact Media.playerCreated player:
  Media.playerCreated.domNodeId -> DOM.getDocument -> DOM.pushNodesByBackendIdsToFrontend -> DOM.getAttributes.
- Inspect only the src attribute of that exact Media player DOM node. Do not inspect page text, scripts, account data, or arbitrary DOM.
- A CELIKOM match still requires an exact approved/entitled signed grant URL, same current Yandex queue track ID, and PLAYING state from that same Media player (kPlay/kPause events only as fallback when kIsPlaying is not exposed).
- If kUrl exists, it remains authoritative; DOM fallback is disabled for that player.
- A blob: MediaSource src, mapping, grant, HTTP 206, network prefetch, or generic playback event alone NEVER proves CELIKOM decoder source.
- Source changes away from the signed CELIKOM URL immediately invalidate the green state.
- No Runtime.evaluate, Network.getResponseBody, extra fetches, or playback commands were added. This is a read-only observer only.
- Raw URLs, src values, tokens, and query strings are never written to diagnostics.

W55 diagnostics now include:
- NativeDomMediaNodeObserved
- NativeDomSourceAttributeObserved
- NativeDomSourceBlobObserved
- NativeDomSourceOtherObserved
- NativeDomSourceAttributeMissingObserved
- NativeDomCelikomSourceMatched

